    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( v \\) such that \\(\\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute the root into the equation:**\n   Let \\( \\alpha = \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\). This root should satisfy the equation \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\).\n\n2. **Substitute \\( x = \\alpha \\) into the equation:**\n   \\[\n   5\\alpha^2 + 21\\alpha + v = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\( \\alpha^2 \\):**\n   \\[\n   \\alpha = \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10}\n   \\]\n   Squaring \\(\\alpha\\):\n   \\[\n   \\alpha^2 = \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right)^2\n   \\]\n   Simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha^2 = \\frac{(-21 - \\sqrt{301})^2}{100}\n   \\]\n   Expand the square:\n   \\[\n   (-21 - \\sqrt{301})^2 = 21^2 + 2 \\cdot 21 \\cdot (-\\sqrt{301}) + (-\\sqrt{301})^2\n   \\]\n   Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   21^2 = 441\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 21 \\cdot (-\\sqrt{301}) = -42\\sqrt{301}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-\\sqrt{301})^2 = 301\n   \\]\n   Combine these results:\n   \\[\n   (-21 - \\sqrt{301})^2 = 441 - 42\\sqrt{301} + 301 = 742 - 42\\sqrt{301}\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha^2 = \\frac{742 - 42\\sqrt{301}}{100}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Substitute back into the equation:**\n   \\[\n   5\\left( \\frac{742 - 42\\sqrt{301}}{100} \\right) + 21\\alpha + v = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5(742 - 42\\sqrt{301})}{100} + 21\\alpha + v = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3710 - 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + 21\\alpha + v = 0\n   \\]\n\n5. **Isolate \\( v \\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3710 - 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} = -21\\alpha - v\n   \\]\n   Multiply both sides by 100 to clear the fraction:\n   \\[\n   3710 - 210\\sqrt{301} = -2100\\alpha - 100v\n   \\]\n   Add \\(2100\\alpha\\) to both sides:\n   \\[\n   3710 = 2100\\alpha - 100v\n   \\]\n   Since \\( \\alpha = \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\), substitute back:\n   \\[\n   -2100 \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right) - 100v = 3710\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   210(21 + \\sqrt{301}) - 100v = 3710\n   \\]\n   Expand:\n   \\[\n   4410 + 210\\sqrt{301} - 100v = 3710\n   \\]\n   Isolate \\( v \\):\n   \\[\n   4410 + 210\\sqrt{301} - 3710 = 100v\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   700 + 210\\sqrt{301} = 100v\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 100:\n   \\[\n   v = \\frac{700 + 210\\sqrt{301}}{100}\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   v = 7 + 2.1\\sqrt{301}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( v \\) is \\boxed{7}.",
